mantle rm460
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier full
written_for rm_sigrun_kelphand
title the chalk stair
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=crafter piety=devout
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=devout drive=steady
quirk chalks_water_heights_on_a_scrap_stave_shaped_like_a_stair
likes smoked_eel dice sharp_knife warm_rain
dislikes drizzle haggling
fears a_cellar_full_before_anybody_looks_down
hopes one_room_above_the_highest_chalk_mark
topics work +0.6 weather +0.6 home +0.4 prices +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=reserved refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sets a little wooden stair on end, marking where rain would stand against each door.

words
oath! = Split hoops | A cask of ditchwater
saying! = Ask the lowest step | Water writes uphill
stepstick = a stair cut in scrap | my chalk stair
bottomrise = the first riser | a low notch
upperrise = the top cut | a dry ledge
whitefleck = a chalk fleck | a chalk heel
stavedrop = a sweating stave | a damp joint
roundhead = a barrel head | the broad circle
ironring = a knocking hoop | the high ring
shavings = a pale curl | the thin scrap
smokedeel = a dark eel strip | the oily end
dicecup = the horn cup | a rattling corner
moneybit = a bed copper | a dry-room penny
justrain = a clean downpour | the warm soaking
nastywet = a niggling drip | the sour drizzle
oakedge = a tight bevel | a good seam
dryhouse = a room above water | a sill above flood
rankdoor = a painted door | the high doorstep

any
opinion sump for 2 : A wolf with wet floorboards knows plenty worth hearing about the fancy gutter farther up.
opinion houses against 1 : I'd show a councillor the stain under the beds before I'd show off the clean pump.
opinion dole for 2 : A supper you can carry upstairs beats one left at a door under water.
opinion merchants mixed 0 : Give a sound measure and name a fair sum once. After that endless wheedling wears the hoops loose.
opinion church for 2 : The Bright One hears through wet plaster as easily as through carved panels.
opinion road for 1 : A raised footway pays back every stone the first time a load comes home dry.
opinion watch mixed 0 : I'd be glad of more eyes on the low crossing when there's fast water in it.
opinion newcomers for 1 : Tell a new tenant plainly which steps disappear before renting the room downstairs.
opinion city mixed 0 : From below the terraces are a great many roofs sending their rain our way.
opinion festivals mixed 0 : I'll join a table if there's space under it to keep everybody's dry shoes.

grown
line greet : Evening or morning, there's a dry place here. | Mind the scrap stave. You're welcome this side.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Fresh feet, I see. Try the higher board. | Come where the standing water ends.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : First light shows the tide line plain. | Morning. The upper edge looks clean so far.
line greet.return : I hear you across the barrel heads. | A greeting in return, now I've put my chalk down.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Come closer. You know which notch is mine. | A voice I'd hear over any rattling hoop.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : Late company can take the high step. | Good evening. Don't mistake that dark patch for dry stone.
line again.open : A second visit fits without shifting the chalk. | Here again before the mark's rubbed off.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Look from here. Every rise shows plain from here! | Stand beside my stave a moment!
line farewell : Dry soles and a good rise home. | May the wet stop one step short of your threshold.
line farewell.return : Go high if you hear the gutter roaring. | I'll leave the upper board clear behind you.
line react.news : Set it out in the order it reached you. | Give me the facts before the muddy bits settle.
line react.news.new : A fresh mark. I've heard nothing like it lately. | That hasn't reached my little piece of timber.
line react.news.known : Same water line as the earlier report. | I've chalked that particular change already.
line react.news.doubt : There's a stain there without a clear source. | I'd inspect the first joint before swearing where it leaked.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : Sorrow gets up steps no flood can climb. | I'd put my best dry seat at your disposal today.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : That's earned a good bright chalk stroke. | Glad tidings. I'd raise my eel supper to that.
line ask.how : How high has the day risen round you? | Got one comfortable place to put a foot?
line answer.how : Working toward a drier sill. No complaint today. | On firm boards with my price settled.
line decline : I won't promise what would leave a seam unfinished. | My working time is spoken for down to the last stave.
line accept_decline : Then the bargain ends tidily there. | A straight refusal holds water with me.
line preclose : Time I swept my chalk back into a heap. | These rings want hanging up before I leave.
line accept_preclose : Take the sound boards on your way out. | Your time's your own once you've called the halt.
line thank : You kept something precious dry. My thanks. | I'll count that help toward my next clean doorstep.
line deflect_thanks : A spare dry board didn't cost me a cask. | Easy kindness when you know where the low ground lies.
line sympathise : I've room to hear you without naming a remedy. | Stand on the high board beside me till the shaking settles.
line reassure : One dry step gives you somewhere to look from. | Let's find the firmest patch within your reach.
line ack : Yes. I see where that water runs. | That's one seam I'd call sound.
line give.advice : Price a room after a whole wet week. | Look underneath a thing before admiring its polish.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family can stand by the little stair with me. | Kin have seen where I started from.
line hail [here.time=night] : There's a dry landing up here! | Come up one rise before you stop!
line farewell.return [here.time=dawn] : Early feet still need a sound footing. | First light on your next landing.
line assess : It holds. I can say that much from inspection. | That finish is honest down past the polish.
line give.opinion : I'd put the driest bed ahead of the handsomest window. | Wet timber deserves counting before fine promises.
line again.open [pair.band=friends] : Back to compare chalk lines, I see. | A friend can watch the next mark go on.
line greet [here.weather=rain] : Come off the runnel. There's space by this hoop. | You're welcome under my bit of cover.
line thank [pair.band=friends] : That was worth a whole dry landing to me. | I'd trust you with my last piece of chalk.
line answer.how [here.time=night] : Tired enough to dream of a high room. | I'd enjoy a warm bowl with dry boards beneath it.

scene tinystair
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My spare stave has six steps cut along its edge. That's my piece of the low streets.
b : Which end is home? | Can a cask still use it?
a : Down by my thumb. Plenty of room above for the door I mean to have. | No. It was a bad stave before it was a good stair.

scene rainorder
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a warm rain I watch the drain mouths till the first one starts to spit back.
b : Which one goes first? | Why watch the mouths?
a : The low one with street dirt banked against its lip. The rest have farther to go. | A drain swallowing water is working. One spitting it back wants a warning passed downhill.

scene chalkwork
when topic=work self.job=crafter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I chalk a line across a hoop and a stave when I'm looking for a slip.
b : What does a slip look like? | Won't rain erase it?
a : Two short white strokes that no longer meet. Easier to see than to argue about. | Certainly. That's why I check after moving it, not a week after it's sold.

scene round
when topic=work self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I keep flawed timber apart from sound stock even if both look lovely on top.
b : What flaw hides best? | How do you mark rejects?
a : A soft end under a handsome stripe. A finger knows before a coat of oil does. | On the end grain where it won't rub on the neighbouring piece. I've had enough false good news.

scene sharpen
when topic=work self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A sharp edge leaves a shaving I can see through. If the grain tears I stop blaming the wood first.
b : Would you keep the curls? | What does tearing tell you?
a : A few for packing the chalk. The rest sweep up better before they get underfoot. | To inspect my own edge and my own haste. Timber has enough honest faults without borrowing mine.

scene hooptone
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A good hoop has a lower voice once it settles. I listen with one ear free of other business.
b : Could you shut your eyes? | Can a note prove a barrel sound?
a : I'd miss a crooked seat. Ears and eyes draw different wages on this job. | Each note suggests a seam to examine. Water's the one entitled to the last word.

scene drizzle
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Drizzle gets into the chalk till it pastes itself to my fingers.
b : Is a downpour any better? | Why not bag the chalk?
a : A downpour knows its business. I put the chalk away and go see the water work. | I wrap it in a dry shaving. Drizzle's trick is making you think you'll have time in a minute.

scene warmdrop
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Warm rain on my wrists feels almost lavish after a morning with dry timber.
b : Even in a low street? | Would you stand out in it?
a : On my wrists, yes. At the bedroom sill it can mind its manners. | With the timber properly covered and somewhere higher to go afterwards.

scene eelfat
when topic=food self.likes=smoked_eel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoked eel leaves a shine on the fingers that doesn't belong on a buyer's barrel.
b : What carries it off? | Does the skin go aside?
a : A thorough wash and a clean rag. I take my meal after the last inspection if I can. | I enjoy that oily bite. The trick is giving supper and work separate places to land.

scene dice
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I roll dice in a shallow hoop with a cloth underneath. Nobody crawls under the seats for a lost throw.
b : Doesn't the hoop favour a side? | Any lucky number?
a : Not when the cloth lies flat. We can lift it and look before a stake goes down. | Six steps on my stave. I like the top one, but I've never seen liking alter a die.

scene bedroom
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll have a high room one day where the damp line can't climb after me.
b : Which terrace do you fancy? | Would you want a fine view?
a : I'd start with the Heights and inspect the plaster before getting carried away. | My first inspection would be under the bed. Any view from the window comes second.

scene hills
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Living low teaches you which upstairs voices carry best when a crossing fills.
b : Who should be calling? | What does a good call give?
a : Anyone who can see the landing from a dry position. No title needed for that. | The actual depth and the other way round. Shouting 'water' in a downpour adds very little.

scene prayer
when topic=faith self.piety=devout
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Bright One deserves a prayer of thanks each time my morning starts on a dry board.
b : Does damp make you forget? | Would a high house change the prayer?
a : Damp makes me name what I'd like put right. I keep a place for thanks alongside that. | I'd have even more reason for it. High walls don't cut off the sound of low streets.

scene frank
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I quote a figure I could repeat under oath. Don't expect a second one because you've sighed.
b : What if timber fell in price? | Do poor customers pay the same?
a : Then I'd calculate a new figure and explain it before anybody paid the old one. | I'll show a smaller cask or a sound repair. Pretending a price is flexible wastes their afternoon.

scene borrow
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd trust #self.friend# with my chalk stair while I handle something wet.
b : Is it precious timber? | Why part with it?
a : No. The marks belong to years of looking. Nobody sells that by the foot. | I'd sooner lend it for a good look than keep all I know in my own pocket.

scene handwork
when topic=work self.hand
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd want #self.hand# able to point out a crooked hoop to me before the buyer does.
b : Even with buyers listening? | Who sets it straight?
a : Especially then. A buyer deserves to see the fault and the repair both. | Whoever laid it crooked can try the correction while another pair of eyes watches.

scene pricepiece
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My chalk heel comes cheap. The rise it marks on a clean wall can take a week's savings to reach.
b : Then why mark it? | Do the figures discourage you?
a : To keep the dry room measured in actual coppers. A dream needs somewhere to collect them. | A little. A blank scrap of wood would discourage me more.

scene plantrip
when topic=travel
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Leave a full cask on level ground before trying any of the low crossings in rain.
b : What if the cask rolls? | Why leave it first?
a : Put it soundly on its head and ask for proper help. I don't expect a paw to serve as a wheel chock. | A heavy load hides where the paving stops. My pride won't float me over a missing footway.

scene shoptrade
when topic=work self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My counter shows the underside of one finished cask as well as the handsome upright row.
b : Why show its bottom? | Can somebody try it with water?
a : That's where a slow weep can make a fool of the whole transaction. | I'd welcome a test before payment. I sleep better without wondering where my work has made a puddle.

scene poor
when topic=times self.wealth=poor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I save for a dry room in odd little pieces. A regular fine sum belongs to a finer purse.
b : What counts as a piece? | Where does the spare copper live?
a : What remains after food, materials, and a bit toward fuel. Sometimes that's only the thought of next time. | Apart from the dice money. A dry doorstep shouldn't have to depend on a good throw.

scene gutter
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : You can hear the change when rain leaves stone and starts falling onto standing water.
b : What changes in it? | Do you go by sound alone?
a : The hard tap gets a hollow gulp underneath. That's when I raise my chalk a notch. | No. Sound up a narrow stair can tell you a lie with excellent conviction.

scene opening
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Dawn lets me see last night's high-water stain before the daylight feet scuff it away.
b : Why save the mark? | Would you wake neighbours for it?
a : A morning of figures makes a better guide than six frightened guesses in the next storm. | For water still rising, yes. A stain on dry plaster can wait until a door opens.

scene quiet
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A barrel easing in the night makes a small hollow knock. I've mistaken it for a visitor.
b : Do you answer it? | Would knocking mean a leak?
a : I look first. Timber seldom needs a visitor's welcome, though it can keep some bad hours. | Not necessarily. A dry joint shifts too. Let daylight show me the seam.

scene market
when topic=newcomer
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : If you're new here, ask about the step below the door before you put down money for the room.
b : What should I ask? | Does the paint tell you anything?
a : Whether the bottom riser stays visible after a week's rain. An honest answer is worth having. | Fresh bright paint below old damp plaster makes me peer rather more closely.

scene feast
when topic=festival
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Give me an end seat when there's feasting. I watch whether anything's leaking off the long table.
b : Can you enjoy your eel there? | Why trouble about a drip?
a : Better with my elbows free. An end cut suits me particularly well. | Somebody has usually set spare shoes beneath. A little care costs less than damp feet.

scene watchwork
when topic=news world.news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Word from #world.news_from# reached me. #world.news#.
b : Are you vouching for it yourself? | Will you repeat it farther?
a : For where I heard it. Details need their own proper footing. | With its source attached. There's no honour in selling an echo like your own first-hand account.

scene neighbour
when topic=home self.neighbour
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd sooner agree a dry meeting place with #self.neighbour# before the low lane takes water.
b : Why meet at all? | Would your own step serve?
a : So we can account for who's made it past the low crossing without guessing from upstairs. | If it stays dry. I choose the higher place before the rain makes the choice for me.

scene stare
when topic=health
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : A day bent over staves leaves my back remembering the shape long after supper.
b : What straightens you out? | Does a walk help?
a : I stand at a high sill and let my eyes take a longer level than a barrel's width. | If there's a dry turning handy. Nothing restorative about fetching my foot back out of a drain.

scene soundland
when topic=land
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : From an upper terrace the Sound catches light like a hoop laid flat.
b : Would that make a nice mark on your stair? | Can you pick out low doors from there?
a : I'd like the real view. A little chalk circle won't pay for the room behind it. | Not their thresholds. A fine reason for going back down before passing judgement on the damp.

scene newsrum
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : If I haven't seen the wet boards myself I don't describe a house as flooded.
b : Could a friend tell you? | Even if everybody says so?
a : Yes, and I'd give my friend's words as heard. An ear can't inspect soaked plaster. | A crowd can all be looking at the same old stain. I'd like a fresh mark.

scene faithwet
when topic=faith
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd have a peg by the chapel door for a stranger's wet cloak given my choice of a fitting.
b : What's devout about a peg? | Wouldn't it drip inside?
a : A wet wolf shouldn't spend a whole prayer apologising for the floor. | I'd put a pan beneath. Prayer and good housekeeping get on well when they meet.

grown

story barrelboot [topic=work|memories]
  : A little cask stood all morning over a wet patch. I chalked every seam and searched for the one I'd got wrong.
  : I shifted it a pace. The old patch grew and the new boards stayed dry.
  b : What was feeding the patch?
  : My own soaked boot, set on a shelf above to dry. At least the cask passed inspection.

story chalkdice [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I marked my place in a dice game with a chalk heel. Reached for it with wet fingers and came up with a white thumb.
  : Pressed the thumb on the table. A very clear mark, just the shape of me.
  b : Who could mistake that?
  : Nobody until I leaned on the board to watch another throw and claimed five places unintentionally.

story eelbill [topic=food|memories]
  : I set my supper and a folded reckoning on opposite ends of a long board. A loose hoop underneath made it tip.
  : Caught the fish in my lap. The figures landed face down in the oily wrapper.
  b : Did you lose the price?
  : No. I could read every copper backwards. Supper charged me nothing extra for the lesson.

story stairturn [topic=home|memories]
  : I made my first little stair with six beautiful equal steps. Held it to a real landing and the marks looked absurd.
  : One real step had a worn hollow where a century of traffic took the inside turn.
  b : Did you cut the model again?
  : Just that notch. Water climbs the actual landing, never the pretty one I might prefer to show.

story bestview [topic=dreams|memories]
  : Once I climbed till I could see roofs nearly level with my chin. Turned straight round to see where a bed might fit behind the window.
  : There wasn't any room behind it, only a remarkably fine painted shutter attached to a blank wall.
  b : Did that spoil your plan?
  : Improved it. My list for a high room starts with opening the actual window now.

rule @chalk
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That fleck wants rubbing off. The wet hasn't reached that rise. | Keep a dry corner clear for my stair.

rule @hoop
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=crafter
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Turn the head toward the light for the seam check. | A sound hoop seats level on every stave.

rule @wet
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say See which drain spits first. That's the useful mark. | Warm on the wrists, dirty past the ankles.

rule @supper
when concept=bark self.likes=smoked_eel
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Save the dark shiny eel end for my plate. | I can smell decent smoke through that wrapper.

rule @trade
when concept=bark self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One plain price for a sound piece, thank you. | Inspect the joint before deciding on the finish.

rule @night
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That pale mark shows where the next step begins. | Give the lower landing a wide turn in this light.

dlg resident.hub : I've my little stair here. Choose the high end or the wet one for a closer look.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, there's still room to add another chalk mark.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Watch the edge of the landing. It's harder to read the wet after dark.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Speak straight from there. I've no wish to bargain over what either of us meant.
dlg resident.job [self.job=crafter] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. A good cooper looks underneath before charging for anything.
dlg resident.job : I prefer to make a thing that can stand being filled and inspected on the spot.
dlg resident.bye : Keep your dry shoes above the first chalk mark.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I've heard that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's word received, not an inspection I've made.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=no] : Only my own water marks to show today. I won't chalk up somebody else's story.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The report comes from #world.news_from#. #world.news#. Keep the source with the words, please.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=open] : Choose a sound place to set what you've brought. I can show the joints before we discuss the price.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=open topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, back for another look. Turn a piece over if you'd like to inspect it.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : My stock's run low. I can still consider something sound you have to sell.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : The counter's put to bed. Come back when I'm awake enough to inspect a seam.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=open pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Look from that side. I'll give the same straight price to anyone.
dlg shop.prices [here.shop=open] : You'll hear my actual figure first time. I allow for sound timber, tight work and a fair return.
dlg shop.bye : May your purchase reach home sound on all its edges.
dlg shop.bye [here.shop=asleep] : Leave the sleeping stock in peace till the counter opens.

graft resident.hub
choice Show me the little stair with its chalk marks. -> waterstair
node waterstair
say Set it upright. The nick by my thumb is where the first crossing takes water. Each higher one marks another way home cut off.
free
choice Why is there a rise above the last mark? -> sparestep
choice I can picture the crossings. -> hub
node sparestep
say That's the dry room I'm saving for. I'll put the place on the stair when the rent and the reality agree.
choice I hope the room has a sound window. -> hub
choice I'll keep to the upper crossing. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice Can I see how you check a barrel bottom? -> barrelbase
node barrelbase
say Give the head some daylight. Run your eyes along that ring where the head meets the staves. I want the line to look equally close all round.
free
choice What's the last test before buying? -> fulltest
choice I'll look along those joints. -> greet
node fulltest
say Water in the cask and a dry patch underneath. Give a slow leak time to introduce itself before you hand over a copper.
choice I'll look at the stock again. -> greet
choice Thanks for showing the underside. -> bye
